            <ArticleTitle>[Spontaneous hematoma and hip pain in a 65-year old patient].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1234-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00108-012-3105-7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The case of a 65-year-old woman with acquired hemophilia is reported. Acquired hemophilia is characterized by the development of inhibitors directed against coagulation factors. Impairment of plasmatic hemostasis leads to a severe bleeding tendency in individuals without a preexisting coagulation defect with considerable mortality. Pathophysiology, diagnostic work-up, and treatment are summarized and discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
